## Definition of Done (project-level)

- [ ] Respects architecture and **layer dependency rules** above.
- [ ] New or changed **public** APIs (use cases, repositories, controllers, hooks) documented briefly where the team expects it.
- [ ] No new linter/analysis issues beyond agreed baselines.
- [ ] Happy path and **major error paths** covered by tests where the project tests that layer.
- [ ] Performance acceptable on target platform (devices, regions, or load profile as applicable).
- [ ] **Accessibility** considered for user-facing UI changes.
- [ ] **Localization** copy is smooth, easy to understand, and user-friendly (see **Localization (l10n / i18n)**).
- [ ] **Security**, **release-time obfuscation** (where applicable), and **pentest-relevant risks** considered for the feature’s scope.
- [ ] **Verbose log, print, and stack-trace diagnostics** are **development-only**, not shipped or executed in production on client or user-visible surfaces.

